IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`
IMPORT `coa8-part15-accounts`

-- coa8-part15-group.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 15, Chapter 4 (annual accounts), Group accounts, ss 399 to 408
-- (lines 5143-5281 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Sections 396(A1), 395(3) to (5) and 396 are called where the text of this Chapter repeats their words for group accounts.
-- Subsections 399(1), 400(6), 401(6) and 408(2) are blank in this text ("...").

§§ `Group accounts`

-- ---- s 399: duty to prepare group accounts -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5152 | (2B) An undertaking falls within this subsection if—
-- src:5153 | (a) it is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom,
-- src:5154 | (b) it has to prepare accounts in accordance with the requirements of this Part of this Act, and
-- src:5155 | (c) it—
-- src:5156 | (i) is an undertaking whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market,
-- src:5157 | (ii) is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council, which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation, or
-- src:5158 | (iii) would be an insurance undertaking within the meaning given by Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC of the European Parliament and of the Council on the annual accounts of insurance undertakings were the United Kingdom a member State.
@ref s 399(2B) An undertaking falling within this subsection (src:5152-5158)
GIVEN `it is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has to prepare accounts in accordance with the requirements of this Part of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it would be an insurance undertaking within the meaning given by Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399(2B) the undertaking falls within this subsection` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An undertaking falls within this subsection if— (a) it is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, (b) it has to prepare accounts in accordance with the requirements of this Part of this Act, and (c)"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a borrowed answer is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` (JUST (`it is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` AND `it has to prepare accounts in accordance with the requirements of this Part of this Act`))
        (`s 362 helper some answer` (LIST JUST `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`,
                                         `it is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation`,
                                         `it would be an insurance undertaking within the meaning given by Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State`))

-- src:5147 | (2A) A company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts if—
-- src:5148 | (a) at the end of the financial year, the company—
-- src:5149 | (i) is subject to the small companies regime, or
-- src:5150 | (ii) would be subject to the small companies regime but for being a public company, and
-- src:5151 | (b) is not a member of a group which, at any time during the financial year, has an undertaking falling within subsection (2B) as a member.
@ref s 399(2A) Exemption for small and would-be small companies (src:5147-5151)
GIVEN `s 381 at the end of the financial year the company is subject to the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 381 at the end of the financial year the company would be subject to the small companies regime but for being a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 399(2B) the undertakings that were members of the group at any time during the financial year and fall within subsection (2B)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399(2A) the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts if"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a seam answer (section 381 or subsection (2B)) is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers`
        (`s 362 helper either answer` `s 381 at the end of the financial year the company is subject to the small companies regime` `s 381 at the end of the financial year the company would be subject to the small companies regime but for being a public company`)
        (`s 362 helper the opposite answer` (`s 362 helper some answer` `s 399(2B) the undertakings that were members of the group at any time during the financial year and fall within subsection (2B)`))

-- src:5159 | (3) There are further exemptions under–
-- src:5160 | section 400 (company included in UK accounts of larger group),
-- src:5161 | section 401 (company included in non-UK accounts of larger group), and
-- src:5162 | section 402 (company none of whose subsidiary undertakings need be included in the consolidation).
@ref s 399(3) Further exemptions under sections 400, 401 and 402 (src:5159-5162)
GIVEN `s 400 the company is exempt under section 400` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 401 the company is exempt under section 401` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 402 the company is exempt under section 402` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399(3) the company is exempt under one of the further exemptions` MEANS
    IF `s 362 helper some answer` (LIST `s 400 the company is exempt under section 400`, `s 401 the company is exempt under section 401`, `s 402 the company is exempt under section 402`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "There are further exemptions under"

-- src:5163 | (4) A company ... which is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts, may do so.
@ref s 399(4) A company that is exempt may nevertheless prepare group accounts (src:5163)
GIVEN `the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399(4) the exempt company may prepare group accounts` MEANS
    IF `the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company ... which is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts, may do so"

-- src:5146 | (2) If at the end of a financial year a company is a parent company the directors, as well as preparing individual accounts for the year, must prepare group accounts for the year unless the company is exempt from that requirement.
@ref s 399(2) Duty to prepare group accounts (src:5146)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) at the end of the financial year the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399(2) the directors are required to prepare group accounts for the year` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at the end of a financial year a company is a parent company the directors ... must prepare group accounts for the year unless the company is exempt from that requirement"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a seam answer is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 1173(1) at the end of the financial year the company is a parent company` (`s 362 helper the opposite answer` `the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts`)

-- ---- s 400 and s 401: exemption for a company included in the group accounts of a larger group ---------------------------------------
-- The cases of subsection (1) are worked out from the allotted shares (a count), the shares the parent undertaking holds, and the shares held by its
-- wholly-owned subsidiaries or on its behalf (which subsection (3) attributes to it).

-- src:5184 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b) and (c) shares held by a wholly-owned subsidiary of the parent undertaking, or held on behalf of the parent undertaking or a wholly-owned subsidiary, shall be attributed to the parent undertaking.
@ref s 400(3) Shares held by a wholly-owned subsidiary or on behalf of the parent are attributed to the parent (src:5184)
GIVEN `the shares held by the parent undertaking` IS A NUMBER
      `the shares held by a wholly-owned subsidiary of the parent undertaking, or on behalf of the parent undertaking or a wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 400(3) the shares attributed to the parent undertaking` MEANS
    `the shares held by the parent undertaking` PLUS `the shares held by a wholly-owned subsidiary of the parent undertaking, or on behalf of the parent undertaking or a wholly-owned subsidiary`

-- src:5186 | (5) Shares held by directors of a company for the purpose of complying with any share qualification requirement shall be disregarded in determining for the purposes of this section whether the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary.
@ref s 400(5) Directors' qualification shares are disregarded in deciding whether the company is wholly-owned (src:5186)
GIVEN `the number of members other than the parent undertaking, its wholly-owned subsidiaries and persons acting on behalf of them` IS A NUMBER
      `of those, the number who hold shares only for the purpose of complying with a share qualification requirement as directors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(5) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the parent undertaking for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the number of members other than the parent undertaking, its wholly-owned subsidiaries and persons acting on behalf of them` MINUS `of those, the number who hold shares only for the purpose of complying with a share qualification requirement as directors` AT MOST 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Shares held by directors of a company for the purpose of complying with any share qualification requirement shall be disregarded in determining for the purposes of this section whether the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary" (a member outside those named remains)

-- src:5166 | (a) where the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of that parent undertaking;
@ref s 400(1)(a) Case (a): a wholly-owned subsidiary (src:5166)
GIVEN `s 400(5) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the parent undertaking for the purposes of this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(1)(a) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of that parent undertaking` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 400(5) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the parent undertaking for the purposes of this section`
    WHEN JUST wholly THEN
        IF wholly
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of that parent undertaking"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:5167 | (b) where that parent undertaking holds 90% or more of the allotted shares in the company and the remaining shareholders have approved the exemption;
@ref s 400(1)(b) Case (b): 90% or more, and the remaining shareholders approve (src:5167)
GIVEN `the allotted shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the shares attributed to the parent undertaking` IS A NUMBER
      `the remaining shareholders have approved the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(1)(b) the parent undertaking holds 90% or more of the allotted shares and the remaining shareholders approve` MEANS
    IF `the allotted shares in the company` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the shares attributed to the parent undertaking` AT LEAST `the allotted shares in the company` TIMES 0.9 AND `the remaining shareholders have approved the exemption`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where that parent undertaking holds 90% or more of the allotted shares in the company and the remaining shareholders have approved the exemption"

-- src:5169 | Such notice must be served at least six months before the end of the financial year to which it relates.
@ref s 400(1) The notice must be served at least six months before the end of the financial year (src:5169)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice was served` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the financial year to which the notice relates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(1) the notice was served in time` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the notice was served` AT MOST `add months` `the last day of the financial year to which the notice relates` (-6)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such notice must be served at least six months before the end of the financial year to which it relates"

-- src:5168 | (c) where that parent undertaking holds more than 50% (but less than 90%) of the allotted shares in the company and notice requesting the preparation of group accounts has not been served on the company by the shareholders holding in aggregate at least 5% of the allotted shares in the company.
@ref s 400(1)(c) Case (c): more than 50% but less than 90%, and no notice from holders of 5% or more (src:5168)
-- `the shares held by shareholders who served a timely notice` counts only a notice that was served in time (see the function above).
GIVEN `the allotted shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the shares attributed to the parent undertaking` IS A NUMBER
      `the shares held by shareholders who served a timely notice requesting the preparation of group accounts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(1)(c) the parent undertaking holds more than 50% but less than 90% of the allotted shares and no sufficient notice has been served` MEANS
    IF `the shares attributed to the parent undertaking` GREATER THAN `the allotted shares in the company` TIMES 0.5 AND `the shares attributed to the parent undertaking` LESS THAN `the allotted shares in the company` TIMES 0.9 AND `the shares held by shareholders who served a timely notice requesting the preparation of group accounts` LESS THAN `the allotted shares in the company` TIMES 0.05
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where that parent undertaking holds more than 50% (but less than 90%) of the allotted shares in the company and notice requesting the preparation of group accounts has not been served on the company by the shareholders holding in aggregate at least 5% of the allotted shares in the company"

-- src:5165 | (1) A company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts if it is itself a subsidiary undertaking and its immediate parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, in the following cases—
-- src:5166 | (a) where the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of that parent undertaking;
-- src:5167 | (b) where that parent undertaking holds 90% or more of the allotted shares in the company and the remaining shareholders have approved the exemption;
-- src:5168 | (c) where that parent undertaking holds more than 50% (but less than 90%) of the allotted shares in the company and notice requesting the preparation of group accounts has not been served on the company by the shareholders holding in aggregate at least 5% of the allotted shares in the company.
@ref s 400(1) Exemption for a company included in the UK group accounts of a larger group (src:5165-5168)
GIVEN `s 1162 the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `its immediate parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `case (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `case (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `case (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(1) the company is within one of the cases that carry the exemption` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts if it is itself a subsidiary undertaking and its immediate parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, in the following cases"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a seam answer is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 1162 the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking`
        (`s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `its immediate parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`)
            (`s 362 helper some answer` (LIST `case (a)`, `case (b)`, `case (c)`)))

-- src:5170 | (2) Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions—
-- src:5171 | (a) the company must be included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom;
-- src:5172 | (b) those accounts must be drawn up and audited, and that parent undertaking's annual report must be drawn up ...—
-- src:5173 | (i) if the undertaking is a company, in accordance with the requirements of this Part of this Act, or, if the undertaking is not a company, the legal requirements which apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking, or
-- src:5174 | (ii) in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards;
-- src:5175 | (c) the company must disclose in the notes to its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts;
-- src:5176 | (d) the company must state in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking that draws up the group accounts referred to above and—
-- src:5177 | (i) the address of the undertaking’s registered office..., or
-- src:5178 | (ii) if it is unincorporated, the address of its principal place of business;
-- src:5179 | (e) the company must deliver to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year in question, copies of—
-- src:5180 | (i) those group accounts, and
-- src:5181 | (ii) the parent undertaking's annual report,
-- src:5182 | together with the auditor's report on them;
-- src:5183 | (f) any requirement of Part 35 of this Act as to the delivery to the registrar of a certified translation into English must be met in relation to any document comprised in the accounts and reports delivered in accordance with paragraph (e).
@ref s 400(2) The conditions of the exemption (src:5170-5183)
GIVEN `the company is included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those accounts are drawn up and audited, and that parent undertaking's annual report is drawn up, in accordance with this Part or the legal requirements for that undertaking or UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company discloses in the notes to its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company states in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking that draws up the group accounts and the address of its registered office or, if it is unincorporated, of its principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company delivers to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year, copies of the group accounts and the parent undertaking's annual report, together with the auditor's report on them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any requirement of Part 35 as to the delivery of a certified translation into English is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(2) the conditions of the exemption are all complied with` MEANS
    IF `the company is included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` AND `those accounts are drawn up and audited, and that parent undertaking's annual report is drawn up, in accordance with this Part or the legal requirements for that undertaking or UK-adopted international accounting standards` AND `the company discloses in the notes to its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts` AND `the company states in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking that draws up the group accounts and the address of its registered office or, if it is unincorporated, of its principal place of business` AND `the company delivers to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year, copies of the group accounts and the parent undertaking's annual report, together with the auditor's report on them` AND `any requirement of Part 35 as to the delivery of a certified translation into English is met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions"

-- src:5185 | (4) The exemption does not apply to a company which is a traded company.
@ref s 400(4) The exemption does not apply to a traded company (src:5185)
GIVEN `s 360C the company is a traded company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(4) the exemption applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 360C the company is a traded company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The exemption does not apply to a company which is a traded company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only withholds the exemption from a traded company

-- src:5189 | (1) A company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts if it is itself a subsidiary undertaking and its parent undertaking is not established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, in the following cases—
-- src:5190 | (a) where the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of that parent undertaking;
