-- src:5193 | Such notice must be served at least six months before the end of the financial year to which it relates.
@ref s 401(1) Exemption for a company included in the non-UK group accounts of a larger group (src:5189-5193)
-- Cases (a) to (c) have the same words as section 400(1)(a) to (c); the same case functions apply.
GIVEN `s 1162 the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `its parent undertaking is not established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `case (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `case (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `case (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(1) the company is within one of the cases that carry the exemption` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts if it is itself a subsidiary undertaking and its parent undertaking is not established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, in the following cases"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a seam answer is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 1162 the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking`
        (`s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `its parent undertaking is not established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`)
            (`s 362 helper some answer` (LIST `case (a)`, `case (b)`, `case (c)`)))

-- src:5194 | (2) Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions—
-- src:5195 | (a) the company and all of its subsidiary undertakings must be included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking;
-- src:5196 | (b) those accounts and, where appropriate, the group’s annual report, must be drawn up—
-- src:5197 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:5198 | (ii) in a manner equivalent to consolidated accounts and consolidated reports drawn up in accordance with the requirements of this Part of this Act,
-- src:5199 | (iii) in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards, or
-- src:5200 | (iv) in accordance with accounting standards which are equivalent to such international accounting standards, as determined pursuant to Commission Regulation (EC) No. 1569/2007 of 21 December 2007 establishing a mechanism for the determination of equivalence of accounting standards applied by third country issuers of securities pursuant to Directives 2003/71/ EC and 2004/109/ EC of the European Parliament and of the Council;
-- src:5201 | (c) the group accounts must be audited by one or more persons authorised to audit accounts under the law under which the parent undertaking which draws them up is established;
-- src:5202 | (d) the company must disclose in its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts;
-- src:5203 | (e) the company must state in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking which draws up the group accounts referred to above and—
-- src:5204 | (i) the address of the undertaking’s registered office (whether in or outside the United Kingdom), or;
-- src:5205 | (ii) if it is unincorporated, the address of its principal place of business;
-- src:5206 | (f) the company must deliver to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year in question, copies of—
-- src:5207 | (i) the group accounts, and
-- src:5208 | (ii) where appropriate, the consolidated annual report,
-- src:5209 | together with the auditor's report on them;
-- src:5210 | (g) any requirement of Part 35 of this Act as to the delivery to the registrar of a certified translation into English must be met in relation to any document comprised in the accounts and reports delivered in accordance with paragraph (f).
@ref s 401(2) The conditions of the exemption (src:5194-5210)
GIVEN `the company and all of its subsidiary undertakings are included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those accounts and, where appropriate, the group's annual report are drawn up in a manner equivalent to this Part, or in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards or equivalent standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group accounts are audited by one or more persons authorised to audit accounts under the law under which the parent undertaking is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company discloses in its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company states in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking that draws up the group accounts and the address of its registered office (whether in or outside the United Kingdom) or, if it is unincorporated, of its principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company delivers to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year, copies of the group accounts and, where appropriate, the consolidated annual report, together with the auditor's report on them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any requirement of Part 35 as to the delivery of a certified translation into English is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(2) the conditions of the exemption are all complied with` MEANS
    IF `the company and all of its subsidiary undertakings are included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking` AND `those accounts and, where appropriate, the group's annual report are drawn up in a manner equivalent to this Part, or in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards or equivalent standards` AND `the group accounts are audited by one or more persons authorised to audit accounts under the law under which the parent undertaking is established` AND `the company discloses in its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts` AND `the company states in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking that draws up the group accounts and the address of its registered office (whether in or outside the United Kingdom) or, if it is unincorporated, of its principal place of business` AND `the company delivers to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year, copies of the group accounts and, where appropriate, the consolidated annual report, together with the auditor's report on them` AND `any requirement of Part 35 as to the delivery of a certified translation into English is met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions"

-- src:5211 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b) and (c), shares held by a wholly-owned subsidiary of the parent undertaking, or held on behalf of the parent undertaking or a wholly-owned subsidiary, are attributed to the parent undertaking.
