    `s 400(5) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the parent undertaking for the purposes of this section` `the number of members other than the parent undertaking, its wholly-owned subsidiaries and persons acting on behalf of them` `of those, the number who hold shares only for the purpose of complying with a share qualification requirement as directors`

-- ---- s 402: exemption if no subsidiary undertakings need be included in the consolidation -------------------------------------------

-- src:5216 | A parent company is exempt from the requirement to prepare group accounts if under section 405 all of its subsidiary undertakings could be excluded from consolidation in Companies Act group accounts.
