    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The group accounts of a parent company that is a charity"

-- src:5226 | (5) There is a relevant change of circumstance if, at any time during or after the first IAS year—
-- src:5227 | (a) the company becomes a subsidiary undertaking of another undertaking that does not prepare IAS group accounts,
-- src:5228 | (b) the company ceases to be a company with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market, or
-- src:5229 | (c) a parent undertaking of the company ceases to be an undertaking with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market.
@ref s 403(5) A relevant change of circumstance (src:5226-5229)
GIVEN `the company becomes a subsidiary undertaking of another undertaking that does not prepare IAS group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company ceases to be a company with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a parent undertaking of the company ceases to be an undertaking with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(5) there is a relevant change of circumstance` MEANS
    IF `the company becomes a subsidiary undertaking of another undertaking that does not prepare IAS group accounts` OR `the company ceases to be a company with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` OR `a parent undertaking of the company ceases to be an undertaking with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "There is a relevant change of circumstance if, at any time during or after the first IAS year"

-- src:5230 | (5A) After a financial year in which the directors of a parent company prepare IAS group accounts for the company, the directors may change to preparing Companies Act group accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance provided they have not changed to Companies Act group accounts in the period of five years preceding the first day of that financial year.
-- src:5231 | (5B) In calculating the five year period for the purpose of subsection (5A), no account should be taken of a change due to a relevant change of circumstance.
@ref s 403(5A) A change to Companies Act group accounts for another reason; (5B) the five-year period (src:5230-5231)
-- The words are those of section 395(4A) and (4B) with "group accounts" for "individual accounts": the same rule is called.
GIVEN `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE
      changes IS A LIST OF `s 395 earlier change to Companies Act accounts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(5A) the directors may change to Companies Act group accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance` MEANS
    `s 395(4A) the directors may change to Companies Act individual accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance` `the first day of the financial year` changes

-- src:5225 | (4) After the first financial year in which the directors of a parent company prepare IAS group accounts (“the first IAS year”), all subsequent group accounts of the company must be prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards unless there is a relevant change of circumstance. This is subject to subsection (5A).
@ref s 403(4) After the first IAS year all subsequent group accounts must be IAS (src:5225)
GIVEN `the directors have already prepared IAS group accounts for an earlier financial year (the first IAS year)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 403(5) there is a relevant change of circumstance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors change to Companies Act group accounts under subsection (5A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 403(5A) the directors may change to Companies Act group accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(4) the directors must prepare IAS group accounts for the financial year` MEANS
    `s 395(3) the directors must prepare IAS individual accounts for the financial year` `the directors have already prepared IAS group accounts for an earlier financial year (the first IAS year)` `s 403(5) there is a relevant change of circumstance` `the directors change to Companies Act group accounts under subsection (5A)` `s 403(5A) the directors may change to Companies Act group accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance`

-- src:5220 | (2) The group accounts of other companies may be prepared—
-- src:5221 | (a) in accordance with section 404 (“Companies Act group accounts”), or
-- src:5222 | (b) in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards (“IAS group accounts”).
-- src:5223 | This is subject to the following provisions of this section.
@ref s 403(2) Group accounts of other companies: the applicable accounting framework (src:5220-5223)
GIVEN framework IS A `s 403(2) accounting framework`
      `s 403(1) the group accounts must be IAS group accounts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 403(3) the group accounts must be Companies Act group accounts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 403(4) the directors must prepare IAS group accounts for the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(2) the group accounts may be prepared in accordance with the framework` MEANS
    -- "The group accounts of other companies may be prepared (a) ... (b) ..." subject to subsections (1), (3) and (4)
    CONSIDER framework
    WHEN `s 403(2)(a) Companies Act group accounts` THEN
        IF `s 403(1) the group accounts must be IAS group accounts` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 403(4) the directors must prepare IAS group accounts for the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 403(2)(b) IAS group accounts` THEN
        IF `s 403(3) the group accounts must be Companies Act group accounts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The group accounts of a parent company that is a charity must be Companies Act group accounts"
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5232 | (6) If, having changed to preparing Companies Act group accounts . . . , the directors again prepare IAS group accounts for the company, subsections (4) and (5) apply again as if the first financial year for which such accounts are again prepared were the first IAS year.
@ref s 403(6) Again preparing IAS group accounts after a change (src:5232)
GIVEN `the directors have changed to preparing Companies Act group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors again prepare IAS group accounts for the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(6) subsections (4) and (5) apply again with the year of the new IAS accounts as the first IAS year` MEANS
    `s 395(5) subsections (3) and (4) apply again with the year of the new IAS accounts as the first IAS year` `the directors have changed to preparing Companies Act group accounts` `the directors again prepare IAS group accounts for the company`

