-- ---- s 405: Companies Act group accounts: subsidiary undertakings included in the consolidation -------------------------------------

-- src:5252 | (2) A subsidiary undertaking may be excluded from consolidation if its inclusion is not material for the purpose of giving a true and fair view (but two or more undertakings may be excluded only if they are not material taken together).
@ref s 405(2) Exclusion because inclusion is not material (src:5252)
GIVEN `its inclusion is not material for the purpose of giving a true and fair view` IS A BOOLEAN
      `two or more undertakings are excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertakings excluded are not material taken together` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(2) the subsidiary undertaking may be excluded from consolidation because its inclusion is not material` MEANS
    -- name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (fork F15): the grant "may be excluded ... if its inclusion is not material" is a grant with an "if" gate, so where the gate fails the text does not say exclusion is barred: NOTHING;
    -- the bracket "two or more undertakings may be excluded only if they are not material taken together" closes its own gate with "only if", so that case stays JUST FALSE
    IF `two or more undertakings are excluded` AND (NOT `the undertakings excluded are not material taken together`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "two or more undertakings may be excluded only if they are not material taken together"
    ELSE IF `its inclusion is not material for the purpose of giving a true and fair view`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A subsidiary undertaking may be excluded from consolidation if its inclusion is not material for the purpose of giving a true and fair view": the grant is stated for a case, and outside it the text does not bar exclusion

-- src:5253 | (3) A subsidiary undertaking may be excluded from consolidation where—
-- src:5254 | (a) severe long-term restrictions substantially hinder the exercise of the rights of the parent company over the assets or management of that undertaking, or
-- src:5255 | (b) extremely rare circumstances mean that the information necessary for the preparation of group accounts cannot be obtained without disproportionate expense or undue delay, or
-- src:5256 | (c) the interest of the parent company is held exclusively with a view to subsequent resale.
@ref s 405(3) Exclusion in three further cases (src:5253-5256)
GIVEN `severe long-term restrictions substantially hinder the exercise of the rights of the parent company over the assets or management of that undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `extremely rare circumstances mean that the information necessary for the preparation of group accounts cannot be obtained without disproportionate expense or undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest of the parent company is held exclusively with a view to subsequent resale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(3) the subsidiary undertaking may be excluded from consolidation in one of the three cases` MEANS
    IF `severe long-term restrictions substantially hinder the exercise of the rights of the parent company over the assets or management of that undertaking` OR `extremely rare circumstances mean that the information necessary for the preparation of group accounts cannot be obtained without disproportionate expense or undue delay` OR `the interest of the parent company is held exclusively with a view to subsequent resale`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A subsidiary undertaking may be excluded from consolidation where"

-- src:5257 | (4) The reference in subsection (3)(a) to the rights of the parent company and the reference in subsection (3)(c) to the interest of the parent company are, respectively, to rights and interests held by or attributed to the company for the purposes of the definition of “parent undertaking” (see section 1162) in the absence of which it would not be the parent company.
@ref s 405(4) The rights and interests referred to in subsection (3)(a) and (c) (src:5257)
GIVEN `the rights or interests are held by or attributed to the company for the purposes of the definition of "parent undertaking" (see section 1162)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the absence of which it would not be the parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(4) the rights or interests count for subsection (3)(a) and (c)` MEANS
    IF `the rights or interests are held by or attributed to the company for the purposes of the definition of "parent undertaking" (see section 1162)` AND `in the absence of which it would not be the parent company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are, respectively, to rights and interests held by or attributed to the company for the purposes of the definition of “parent undertaking” (see section 1162) in the absence of which it would not be the parent company"

-- src:5251 | (1) Where a parent company prepares Companies Act group accounts, all the subsidiary undertakings of the company must be included in the consolidation, subject to the following exceptions.
@ref s 405(1) All subsidiary undertakings must be included, subject to the exceptions (src:5251)
GIVEN `the parent company prepares Companies Act group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1162 the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary undertaking may be excluded under subsection (2) or (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(1) the subsidiary undertaking must be included in the consolidation` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a parent company prepares Companies Act group accounts, all the subsidiary undertakings of the company must be included in the consolidation, subject to the following exceptions"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a seam answer is not known and no limb decides
    IF NOT `the parent company prepares Companies Act group accounts`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `s 362 helper both answers` `s 1162 the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the company` exceptionNotShown
    WHERE
        -- a NOTHING from the exceptions means no exception is shown (the grant of subsection (2) answers NOTHING where its "if" is unmet, fork F15), so "all the subsidiary undertakings ... must be included" stands
        exceptionNotShown MEANS
            CONSIDER `the subsidiary undertaking may be excluded under subsection (2) or (3)`
            WHEN JUST excepted THEN JUST (NOT excepted)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE

