    CONSIDER frameworks
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN all (GIVEN f YIELD f EQUALS first) rest

-- src:5267 | (1) The directors of a parent company must secure that the individual accounts of—
-- src:5268 | (a) the parent company, and
-- src:5269 | (b) each of its subsidiary undertakings,
-- src:5270 | are all prepared using the same financial reporting framework, except to the extent that in their opinion there are good reasons for not doing so.
@ref s 407(1) The directors of a parent company must secure the same financial reporting framework (src:5267-5270)
-- "the individual accounts of (a) the parent company, and (b) each of its subsidiary undertakings, are all prepared using the same financial reporting
-- framework, except to the extent that in their opinion there are good reasons for not doing so". Subsection (2) (no group accounts), (3) (accounts not
-- required under this Part), (4) (charities against non-charities) and (5) (the parent's own accounts when IAS group and IAS individual accounts are prepared) narrow it.
GIVEN `the directors prepare group accounts for the parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the parent company prepare IAS group accounts and IAS individual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      parent IS A `s 407 individual accounts of an undertaking`
      `the subsidiary undertakings` IS A LIST OF `s 407 individual accounts of an undertaking`
      `in their opinion there are good reasons for not doing so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 407(1) the directors have secured that the individual accounts are prepared using the same financial reporting framework` MEANS
    IF NOT `the directors prepare group accounts for the parent company`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- subsection (2): subsection (1) does not apply, so there is nothing to secure (fork F3)
    ELSE IF `in their opinion there are good reasons for not doing so` OR (`s 407(1) all the frameworks are the same` (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 407 the financial reporting framework`) charityAccounts) AND `s 407(1) all the frameworks are the same` (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 407 the financial reporting framework`) otherAccounts))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of a parent company must secure that the individual accounts of— (a) the parent company, and (b) each of its subsidiary undertakings, are all prepared using the same financial reporting framework, except to the extent that in their opinion there are good reasons for not doing so"
    WHERE
        -- (3): only accounts of subsidiary undertakings required to be prepared under this Part; (5): the parent's own accounts are left out in the IAS and IAS case
        relevant MEANS append (IF `the directors of the parent company prepare IAS group accounts and IAS individual accounts` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST parent) (filter (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 407 the accounts are required to be prepared under this Part`) `the subsidiary undertakings`)
        -- (4): a charity's accounts are compared only with other charities' accounts
        charityAccounts MEANS filter (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 407 the undertaking is a charity`) relevant
        otherAccounts MEANS filter (GIVEN a YIELD NOT a's `s 407 the undertaking is a charity`) relevant

-- ---- s 408: individual profit and loss account where group accounts prepared -------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5276 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:5277 | (a) a company prepares group accounts in accordance with this Act, and
-- src:5278 | (b) the company’s individual balance sheet shows the company’s profit and loss for the financial year determined in accordance with this Act.
@ref s 408(1) Where section 408 applies (src:5276-5278)
GIVEN `the company prepares group accounts in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's individual balance sheet shows the company's profit and loss for the financial year determined in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 408(1) section 408 applies` MEANS
    IF `the company prepares group accounts in accordance with this Act` AND `the company's individual balance sheet shows the company's profit and loss for the financial year determined in accordance with this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) a company prepares group accounts in accordance with this Act, and (b) the company's individual balance sheet shows the company's profit and loss"

-- src:5280 | (3) The company's individual profit and loss account must be approved in accordance with section 414(1) (approval by directors) but may be omitted from the company's annual accounts for the purposes of the other provisions of the Companies Acts.
@ref s 408(3) The individual profit and loss account may be omitted from the annual accounts (src:5280)
GIVEN `s 408(1) section 408 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 408(3) the individual profit and loss account may be omitted from the company's annual accounts for the purposes of the other provisions of the Companies Acts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 408(1) section 408 applies`
    WHEN JUST applies THEN
        IF applies
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (section 408 does not apply, so there is no exemption)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:5280 | (3) The company's individual profit and loss account must be approved in accordance with section 414(1) (approval by directors) but may be omitted from the company's annual accounts for the purposes of the other provisions of the Companies Acts.
@ref s 408(3) The individual profit and loss account must be approved under section 414(1) (src:5280)
GIVEN `the individual profit and loss account has been approved in accordance with section 414(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 408(3) the individual profit and loss account has been approved as section 408(3) requires` MEANS
    IF `the individual profit and loss account has been approved in accordance with section 414(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company's individual profit and loss account must be approved in accordance with section 414(1)"

-- src:5281 | (4) The exemption conferred by this section is conditional upon its being disclosed in the company's annual accounts that the exemption applies.
@ref s 408(4) The exemption is conditional on disclosure (src:5281)
GIVEN `it is disclosed in the company's annual accounts that the exemption applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 408(4) the exemption conferred by section 408 is available` MEANS
    IF `it is disclosed in the company's annual accounts that the exemption applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The exemption conferred by this section is conditional upon its being disclosed in the company's annual accounts that the exemption applies"
